and contributors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The Federal District (CAESB) problem formulation and input data are derived
from the work of A. P. Giacomazzo (Universidade de Brasília, 2020) and
B. M. Araújo, D. F. Gold, L. B. Lau, P. M. Reed and C. M. A. Alves (2024),
https://github.com/lbl59/federal_district (doi:10.5281/zenodo.8221350).

Modifications by Aseel Mohamed (2025-2026) include: the WaterSupplySystems
class and multi-subsystem Utility architecture; per-WSS risk-of-failure,
infrastructure management and financial accounting; WSS-level restrictions
with tariff surcharges, bilateral transfers with sender demand protection and
the EmergencyTransferParanoa policy; WSS-level reliability, affordability and
severity objectives with experiment modes 1-8; new data collectors and
outputs. Files changed relative to the original are listed in CHANGELOG.md.

This product includes QuadProg++ (src/Utils/QPSolver), distributed under its
own license. Borg MOEA (Copyright The Pennsylvania State University) is NOT
included and must be obtained separately from http://borgmoea.org.
